chapter HOPAT

session HOPAT = HOL +
  description \<open>
    Higher-order pattern unification (Nipkow's algorithm) on de Bruijn
    lambda-terms: termination and correctness (most general unifiers for
    well-typed patterns), following Grobauer's pen-and-paper proofs.
    Also contains the substitution lemma in three styles (de Bruijn, Nominal,
    Nominal2) for comparison.
  \<close>
  sessions
    "HOL-Library"
    "HOL-Nominal"
    "HOL-Proofs-Lambda"
    Nominal2
  theories
    Partial_Termination
    DeBruijn_Substitution_Lemma
    Nominal_Substitution_Lemma
    Nominal2_Substitution_Lemma
    Unif_Termination
    Unif_Correctness
  document_files
    "root.bib"
    "root.tex"
